    "body": "Coverity detected a resource leak in the function encode_vim_to_lua generated from src/nvim/eval/typval_encode.c.h. From coverity's description:\r\n\r\nThe system resource will not be reclaimed and reused, reducing the future availability of the resource. In encode_vim_to_lua: Leak of memory or pointers to system resources\r\n\r\nTYPVAL_ENCODE_CONV_LIST_START and TYPVAL_ENCODE_CONV_DICT_START in src/nvim/lua/converter.c return directly when lua_checkstack() fails. When they are expanded in the main encode_vim_to_* loop (for partial arguments and self dict) rather than in convert_one_value, this skips kvi_destroy() and leaks mpstack once it has grown beyond its inline storage. The JSON encoder's TYPVAL_ENCODE_CONV_STRING has the same problem for dict keys that are not valid UTF-8.\r\n\r\nAdd an encode_vim_to__error_ret label to convert_one_value as well, so it is common to both functions, and make these macros jump to it instead of returning.\r\n\r\nAI-assisted\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n  Thank you for contributing to Neovim!\r\n  If this is your first time, check out https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-requests-prs\r\n  for our PR guidelines.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nCoverity CID 530030: resource leak in `encode_vim_to_lua`.\r\n\r\nSome `TYPVAL_ENCODE_*` macros `return` on error. When they expand in the\r\nmain `encode_vim_to_*` loop instead of in `convert_one_value`, they skip\r\n`kvi_destroy()`, which leaks `mpstack` once it has grown past its inline\r\nstorage:\r\n\r\n- Lua: `TYPVAL_ENCODE_CONV_LIST_START`/`DICT_START` when `lua_checkstack()`\r\n  fails while converting partial args/self (the case Coverity reported).\r\n- JSON: `TYPVAL_ENCODE_CONV_STRING` on a dict key that isn't valid UTF-8.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nAdd an `encode_vim_to__error_ret` label to `convert_one_value` too, so\r\nboth functions have it (like `typval_encode_stop_converting_one_item`),\r\nand make these macros jump to it instead of returning.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-01T22:43:18Z",
